---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Accessibility', path: '/accessibility/' },
];
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Page
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description="Our accessibility commitment for kirbychanmarkham.com, the WCAG 2.1 AA standard we build to, known limitations and how to request an accessible format."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Accessibility statement"
  accent="Accessibility"
  lede={`What we build to, what we have done, what is still outstanding and how to ask for information in another format. Last updated ${updated}.`}
  crumbs={crumbs}
  tone="sand"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <h2>Our commitment</h2>
      <p>
        Kirby Chan &amp; Co. Real Estate Team is committed to providing services in a way that
        respects the dignity and independence of people with disabilities, consistent with the
        Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act and the Ontario Human Rights Code.
      </p>
      <p>
        We build this website to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines version 2.1 at Level
        AA.
      </p>

      <h2>What we have done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Semantic HTML, with headings in order and landmarks on every page</li>
        <li>A skip to content link as the first item in the tab order</li>
        <li>Visible focus indicators on every interactive element</li>
        <li>
          Text and background colour combinations checked against the 4.5 to 1 contrast ratio for
          body text. Our gold accent is used only for decoration and large display type on light
          backgrounds because it does not meet that ratio at small sizes
        </li>
        <li>Navigation that works entirely with a keyboard, including the neighbourhood menu</li>
        <li>
          A scrolling market band that respects the reduced motion setting in your operating system
          and that is duplicated as plain text in reading order for assistive technology
        </li>
        <li>Video embeds that load only when you choose to play them, with descriptive link text</li>
        <li>Form fields with real labels, clear error messages and a status message region</li>
        <li>Touch targets of at least 44 by 44 pixels on interactive controls</li>
        <li>Text that reflows without horizontal scrolling down to a 320 pixel viewport</li>
        <li>A schematic map that is duplicated as a text list of the same links</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <p>We are being specific about these rather than claiming the site is perfect.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Video transcripts and captions are not yet available for every video. We are adding them
          as videos are published. In the meantime, ask us and we will provide a written summary.
        </li>
        <li>
          Property search is provided by a third party system that we do not control. If you have
          difficulty using it, contact us and we will run the search for you and send you the
          results in a format that works for you.
        </li>
        <li>
          Our spam filtering uses Cloudflare Turnstile. If it creates a barrier for you, phone or
          email us instead and we will take your enquiry directly.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Alternative formats</h2>
      <p>
        If you need information from this site in another format, such as large print, plain text
        or read aloud over the phone, ask us and we will provide it at no extra cost. We will agree
        a suitable format with you.
      </p>

      <h2>Feedback</h2>
      <p>
        If you run into a barrier on this site, we want to know. Email {site.contact.email} or
        phone {site.contact.phone}. Tell us the page and what happened and we will reply and
        explain what we are doing about it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Feedback can be given by email, by phone or in person, whichever suits you. We will
        acknowledge it and respond in the same format unless you ask for another.
      </p>

      <h2>Testing</h2>
      <p>
        <span class="todo-badge">
          TODO: record the date of the last accessibility audit, the tools used and who carried it
          out, then list the results here
        </span>
      </p>
      <p>
        We test with keyboard navigation, automated checks and screen reader spot checks. Automated
        tools catch only part of what matters, so the feedback address above is a genuine part of
        how we find problems.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
